I go inside the large metro station.
This station is very spacious.
I go towards the ticket counter.
A worker is sitting there.
I say to him, "Hello, sir."
He says, "Hello, madam, tell me."
I say, "I need to get to the station near the sea."
"I want to travel by metro every day now."
"So I want a permanent metro card."
He says, "Yes, you will definitely get it."
"One hundred rupees for the card and one hundred rupees for the journey."
"So it takes two hundred rupees in total."
I take money out of my purse.
I give him two hundred rupees.
He gives me a new metro card.
I take the card.
I say to him, "Thank you, sir."
I safely keep my new card in my bag.
Now I need to get to the platform.
And I need to board the metro train.
